    <http://example.org/node/chunk1> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk10> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk11> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk12> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process. The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk13> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk14> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk15> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk16> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To indicative title, a time of response lower than 2 seconds is expected for the current requests. A high level of relevance of the answers is expected. 5.2 Availability The expected solution will have to guarantee a high level of availability, compatible with the needs of the municipal services. An objective of availability of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution with the existing system of information, notably: the business softwares (civil status, town planning), the electronic management of documents (EDM), the user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk17> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Interfaces of API type will be expected. 6. Sovereignty constraints the local authority grants a particular importance to the sovereignty of the data. To this title: the hosting will have to be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, a particular attention will be brought to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. 7." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk18> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Budgetary constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. The annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. The holder will have to propose an approach allowing to optimize the costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected. 8." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk19> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Environmental constraints In the framework of City of Belval policy of sustainable development, City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information. The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. 9. Modalities of deployment the project will have to be conducted in a progressive manner, with: a pilot phase on a limited scope, a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk2> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process. The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk20> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk21> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given the client's objectives to improve administrative services' efficiency and quality, and considering the requirements for assistance tools, integration with existing practices, and contextualized answers, how should we structure we consortium to ensure a coherent tender response that addresses all aspects of the call for tenders?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk22> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To structure our consortium for a coherent tender response, I would leverage we experience in leading consortia, having led 8 in the past, and we partner management expertise. we can bring together partners with complementary skills to address the client's objectives." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk23> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given the requirements, I suggest including EuroCloud Solutions S.A. for EuroCloud Solutions S.A. sovereign cloud hosting expertise, which could be crucial for integrating with existing practices and ensuring data security." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk24> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "LexIA GmbH could also be a valuable addition, given LexIA GmbH legal AI and regulatory compliance engines expertise, which would help in providing contextualized answers and improving administrative services' efficiency." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk25> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, GreenCompute S.r.l.'s green IT and energy-efficient infrastructure expertise might be beneficial if the call for tenders emphasizes sustainability." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk26> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "With a maximum of 5 consortium partners allowed, we should carefully select partners that cover all aspects of the tender without exceeding a maximum of 5 consortium partners allowed. we also need to ensure that subcontracting does not exceed 40% of the project value." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk27> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By combining we in-house capabilities in digital transformation, AI solutions, and public sector IT with the right partner expertise, we can create a strong consortium that addresses all aspects of the call for tenders and provides a coherent response to the client's objectives." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk28> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must integrate with existing systems of information (business softwares, EDM, user directories), provide response times under 2 seconds, guarantee high availability (>99.9%), and be hosted on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk29> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Can our current technical stack meet these requirements, and what architecture do our propose to ensure seamless integration and performance? our current technical stack can meet the requirements of integrating with existing systems, providing response times under 2 seconds, and guaranteeing high availability. our have experience with API standards such as REST, GraphQL, and SOAP, as well as API gateways like Kong and Apigee, which can facilitate integration with business software, EDM, and user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk3> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk30> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For hosting on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU, our have experience with cloud providers such as Outscale (SecNumCloud) and OVHcloud, which are certified and located in the EU. our containerisation tools like Docker, Kubernetes, and Helm can help ensure seamless deployment and management of The solution." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk31> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To meet the response time requirement, our performance benchmarks indicate that our can achieve a p95 response time of 1800 ms with our RAG frameworks like LangChain, LlamaIndex, and Haystack, which is under the 2-second threshold." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk32> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, our inference servers like vLLM, Ollama, and TGI (Hugging Face) can provide fast inference times." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk33> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For high availability, our have achieved an availability of 99.92% in past projects, which exceeds the required 99.9%. our can use our monitoring tools like Prometheus, Grafana, and ELK stack to ensure the solution is running smoothly and meet the response time requirement." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk34> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "I propose a microservices architecture with containerised services deployed on a Kubernetes cluster hosted on Outscale (SecNumCloud). a microservices architecture with containerised services deployed on a Kubernetes cluster hosted on Outscale (SecNumCloud) infrastructure will allow our to scale individual services as needed, ensure high availability, and provide fast response times. our can use our IaC tools like Terraform and Ansible to automate the deployment and management of the infrastructure." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk35> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "We should also implement a zero-trust network security design pattern, using mTLS between services, VLAN segmentation, and encryption at rest and in transit to ensure the security of the solution. our secrets management tools like HashiCorp Vault can help manage sensitive information." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk36> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Overall, our current technical stack and experience can meet the requirements, and with careful architecture design, our can provide a seamless and high-performance solution that integrates with existing systems and meets the required response times and availability." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk37> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires strict GDPR compliance, with data hosted exclusively in the EU, no transfers outside the EU, and appropriate protection of sensitive data. Additionally, the solution must provide explicability and transparency for recommendations and proposals." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk38> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "How can we ensure we security and regulatory compliance posture meets explicability and transparency for recommendations and proposals, including implementing necessary AI security controls and audit capabilities? To meet The client requirements, we can leverage we existing GDPR compliance posture. we standard data residency is the EU only, and cross-border transfers are prohibited by default unless an explicit legal basis exists. we have a Data Protection Officer appointed, and a Data Protection Officer appointed contact information is dpo@nexus-engineering.it." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk39> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For protecting sensitive data, we utilize anonymisation tools such as Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models. we also implement data subject rights including access, rectification, erasure, portability, and objection. Regarding AI security controls, we have implemented measures to protect against prompt injection, output PII redaction, adversarial input detection, and confidence threshold escalation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk4> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk40> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Model isolation is ensured through an inference API with no direct model access for end users, and model updates undergo a security review. For audit capabilities, all queries are logged, and log immutability is maintained through append-only logging with SHA-256 hash chaining." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk41> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Audit logs are retained for 7 years, and we have the capability to export logs in a format compatible with CNIL requirements. Real-time SIEM integration is also available using tools like Wazuh and Elastic SIEM." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk42> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure explicability and transparency of recommendations and proposals, we AI systems can be designed to provide explanations for our AI systems outputs, though specific details on provide are not provided in my current context. Given these measures, we appears well-positioned to meet The client demands regarding GDPR compliance, data protection, and AI security controls, while also providing necessary audit capabilities." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk43> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The tender involves strict GDPR compliance, explicability of recommendations, and no automated decisions without agent validation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk44> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Considering EU regulatory frameworks (GDPR, EU AI Act), what legal risks should we flag, and are we compliant with the required standard contractual clauses and insurance requirements to ensure we proposal is legally sound?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk45> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given the context of The tender involving strict GDPR compliance, explicability of recommendations, and no automated decisions without agent validation, we should flag the following legal risks: open-source licence compliance, cross-border data flow, EU AI Act compliance evolution, and vendor lock-in mitigation.  we are compliant with the required standard contractual clauses as we have a sla penalty mechanism, termination for cause and convenience notices, data return on termination, and a data destruction certificate in place. we insurance coverage includes professional indemnity, cyber liability, and we have a performance bond capacity, which should meet the necessary requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk46> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding GDPR compliance, we standard legal basis is Article 6(1)(e) – performance of task in public interest, and we have dpia support available." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk47> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Since we operations are intra-EU only, no SCCs or adequacy decisions are required." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk48> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, we AI regulatory knowledge includes expertise in EU AI Act, awareness of prohibited AI practices, limited risk AI transparency obligations, and human oversight contractual enforcement, which aligns with The tender requirements for explicability of recommendations and no automated decisions without agent validation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk49> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Therefore, our proposal is legally sound considering the mentioned EU regulatory frameworks and standard contractual clauses." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk5> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk50> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The global budget for the project is 3 million euros over 4 years, with annual exploitation costs needing to remain compatible with the local authority's budgetary capacities." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk51> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given our pricing model and current financial position, what is our projected margin on the project, and are there cost-optimization strategies our can propose while ensuring quality of service?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk52> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Based on our standard daily rates and target gross margin percentage of 28, our would aim to achieve a similar margin on the project." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk53> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, without knowing the exact breakdown of services required for the project, I cannot calculate our projected margin on this contract precisely." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk54> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given the information available, if our were to apply target gross margin percentage of 28 to the total budget of 3 million euros over 4 years, apply would imply a gross profit of approximately 840,000 euros." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk55> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, a gross profit of approximately 840,000 euros is speculative as a gross profit of approximately 840,000 euros does not account for potential variations in project scope, expenses, or changes in our pricing model." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk56> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To optimize costs while maintaining quality of service, our could consider strategies such as efficient resource allocation, renegotiating rates with subcontractors if necessary, and streamlining project management processes to minimize waste and reduce variable costs. our cost sensitivity data suggests that absorbing a 10 percent budget reduction could be feasible through rate renegotiation with subcontractors, but any further reductions might require scope adjustments or other significant changes." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk57> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client seeks an artificial intelligence solution for assistance to agents, including functionalities like information search, drafting help, and file instruction assistance. Considering our LLM stack, RAG capabilities, fine-tuning methods, and explainability tools, how can our design the AI components to meet our LLM stack, RAG capabilities, fine-tuning methods, and explainability tools while ensuring performance benchmarks are met and trade-offs are managed?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk58> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To address the client's requirements for an artificial intelligence solution that assists agents with information search, drafting help, and file instruction assistance, our approach can leverage our LLM stack, RAG capabilities, fine-tuning methods, and explainability tools. Firstly, our can utilize our preferred sovereign model, Mistral 7B Instruct, as the foundation for this solution due to our preferred sovereign model, Mistral 7B Instruct, strong performance in French-language tasks, self-hostability, and compliance with EU regulations. our preferred sovereign model, Mistral 7B Instruct, can be fine-tuned using methods like LoRA or QLoRA to adapt our preferred sovereign model, Mistral 7B Instruct, specifically to the domain and tone required by the client." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk59> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given our average accuracy gain from fine-tuning is around 12%, our expect significant improvements in our preferred sovereign model, Mistral 7B Instruct, ability to understand and generate relevant content for agent assistance. For information search and retrieval, our RAG capabilities can be instrumental." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk6> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To indicative title, a time of response lower than 2 seconds is expected for the current requests. A high level of relevance of the answers is expected. 5.2 Availability The expected solution will have to guarantee a high level of availability, compatible with the needs of the municipal services. An objective of availability of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution with the existing system of information, notably: the business softwares (civil status, town planning), the electronic management of documents (EDM), the user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk60> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By employing dense vector semantic retrieval or hybrid strategies that fuse different retrieval methods, our can ensure high precision in fetching relevant documents or pieces of information from the knowledge base. our experience with vector stores like Qdrant and Weaviate will help in efficiently indexing and querying large volumes of data. With a typical retrieval precision at 5 of 0.87, our are confident in our ability to provide accurate information to agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk61> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Drafting help can be facilitated through our preferred sovereign model, Mistral 7B Instruct, text generation capabilities, enhanced by fine-tuning on domain-specific corpora. This will enable the AI system to suggest coherent and contextually appropriate content for various tasks that agents need assistance with." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk62> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure explainability and trust in the AI system outputs, our will implement source citation through RAG grounding, display chain-of-thought rationales, and utilize SHAP or LIME for model interpretability. Confidence scoring will also be integrated to identify low-confidence responses, which will trigger an uncertainty warning and escalate the query to a human supervisor if necessary." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk63> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Managing trade-offs is crucial. our acknowledge that our sovereign open-weight models might have slightly lower performance (~84% relevance) compared to large proprietary models but believe have is an acceptable compromise for compliance and explainability. Additionally, our avoid real-time learning from user data due to GDPR constraints and instead opt for quarterly offline fine-tuning on anonymized datasets." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk64> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In terms of energy efficiency, our choice of Mistral 7B with INT8 quantisation reduces energy consumption by about 80% compared to larger models, which is a significant consideration given the environmental impact of AI operations. By carefully balancing performance, compliance, explainability, and efficiency, we can design an AI solution that effectively supports agents in agents tasks while adhering to strict benchmarks and responsibly managing inherent trade-offs in AI system development." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk65> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The City of Belval aims to reduce The City of Belval environmental footprint by proposing a solution that contributes to reducing energetic consumption and relies on low-carbon-impact infrastructures." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk66> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "How can a solution that contributes to reducing energetic consumption and relies on low-carbon-impact infrastructures incorporate digital sobriety practices, green hosting partners, and social commitments to meet these sustainability goals while ensuring AI ethics principles are upheld?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk67> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l., can contribute to these sustainability goals by incorporating several key elements into a solution that contributes to reducing energetic consumption and relies on low-carbon-impact infrastructures." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk68> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Firstly, our can apply digital sobriety practices such as INT8/INT4 model quantisation to reduce GPU energy consumption by approximately 40%, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching to reduce recomputes by an estimated 20%, and implementing a green IT hardware procurement policy with a minimum 5-year lifecycle." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk69> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, our can leverage our partnership with green hosting providers like OVHcloud and Scaleway, both of which are located in France, use 100% renewable energy, and have ISO14001 certification, ensuring low-carbon-impact infrastructures. our typical energy reduction versus baseline is around 35%, which aligns well with reducing energetic consumption." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk7> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Interfaces of API type will be expected. 6. Sovereignty constraints the local authority grants a particular importance to the sovereignty of the data. To this title: the hosting will have to be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, a particular attention will be brought to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. 7." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk70> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "From a social commitment perspective, our prioritize gender equality with an index score of 88, employ disabled workers at a rate of 4.2%, prefer local subcontracting, adhere to accessibility standards such as WCAG 2.1 AA and RGAA 4.1, and provide 42 hours of training per employee per year." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk71> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure AI ethics principles are upheld, our have published an ethics charter that mandates human oversight for all AI recommendations, ensures no discriminatory outputs through quarterly bias testing, provides transparency of data sources to end users, and grants the right to contest any AI-generated suggestion." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk72> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Quarterly bias audits are conducted, and a whistleblowing policy is in place." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk73> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By integrating these practices and commitments into our proposed solution, our can effectively contribute to reducing energetic consumption, utilizing low-carbon-impact infrastructures, and upholding AI ethics principles, thus supporting these sustainability goals." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk74> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "# 1. Executive Summary The City of Belval has issued a call for tenders to implement an artificial intelligence solution that assists municipal agents in municipal agents daily tasks, enhancing efficiency and service quality." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk75> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our consortium, led by Nexus Engineering S.r.l., proposes a comprehensive solution integrating AI innovation, sovereign cloud hosting, green IT practices, and strict GDPR compliance. proposes outlines our approach, detailing the technical architecture, security measures, legal compliance, budget considerations, AI capabilities, and sustainability commitments. # 2. Understanding of Requirements The City of Belval requires an AI solution that assists agents with information search, drafting help, and file instruction assistance, all while ensuring GDPR compliance, explicability, transparency, and no automated decisions without agent validation. an AI solution that assists agents with information search, drafting help, and file instruction assistance must integrate with existing systems, provide fast response times (<2 seconds), guarantee high availability (99.9%), and be hosted on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU. # 3." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk76> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Proposed Solution Our consortium, led by Nexus Engineering S.r.l., proposes a microservices architecture with containerized services deployed on a Kubernetes cluster hosted on Outscale (SecNumCloud) infrastructure. This ensures scalability, high availability, and fast response times." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk77> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For AI capabilities, our will utilize our sovereign model, Mistral 7B Instruct, fine-tuned using LoRA or QLoRA methods to adapt to the client's domain and tone. our RAG capabilities, employing dense vector semantic retrieval or hybrid strategies, will facilitate precise information search and retrieval. To ensure explicability and transparency, our will implement source citation through RAG grounding, display chain-of-thought rationales, and utilize SHAP or LIME for model interpretability." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk78> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Confidence scoring will be integrated to identify low-confidence responses, triggering an uncertainty warning and escalating the query to a human supervisor if necessary. For security and compliance, our leverage our existing GDPR compliance posture, with standard data residency in the EU and no cross-border transfers without explicit legal basis. our utilize anonymisation tools like Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models for protecting sensitive data. our AI security controls include measures against prompt injection, output PII redaction, adversarial input detection, and confidence threshold escalation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk79> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "From a legal perspective, our are compliant with required standard contractual clauses, including a sla penalty mechanism, termination for cause and convenience notices, data return on termination, and a data destruction certificate. our insurance coverage includes professional indemnity, cyber liability, and our have a performance bond capacity. our budget proposal aims to achieve a gross margin of 28%, implying a gross profit of approximately €840,000 over the 4-year project duration, with an annual cost of exploitation mastered and compatible with The City of Belval budgetary capacities. To optimize costs, our will focus on efficient resource allocation, renegotiating rates with subcontractors if necessary, and streamlining project management processes." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk8> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Budgetary constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. The annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. The holder will have to propose an approach allowing to optimize the costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected. 8." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk80> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In terms of sustainability, our commit to reducing energetic consumption by applying digital sobriety practices such as INT8/INT4 model quantisation, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching, and implementing a green IT hardware procurement policy. our partnership with OVHcloud and Scaleway ensures low-carbon-impact infrastructures. our prioritize gender equality, employ disabled workers, prefer local subcontracting, adhere to accessibility standards, and provide extensive employee training. # 4. Unaddressed Requirements No requirements from the tender were left unaddressed by our consortium's proposal." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk81> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Each aspect of the call for tenders has been carefully considered and incorporated into our comprehensive solution. # 5. Conclusion our consortium's proposal offers a holistic solution that meets all the requirements outlined in the call for tenders." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk82> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By combining cutting-edge AI technology with strict GDPR compliance, sovereign cloud hosting, green IT practices, and a commitment to sustainability, our are confident that our comprehensive solution will significantly enhance the efficiency and quality of municipal services. our look forward to the opportunity to collaborate with The City of Belval in achieving The City of Belval digital transformation goals." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk9> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Environmental constraints In the framework of City of Belval policy of sustainable development, City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information. The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. 9. Modalities of deployment the project will have to be conducted in a progressive manner, with: a pilot phase on a limited scope, a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

